          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-14 22:59:25.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20860 doc: add more agent workflow guidance",
        "message": "LU-20860 doc: add more agent workflow guidance\n\nAdd guidance that came up in recent patch work: when to start looking\nfor existing work, how to split and restack patches, which CI\nfollow-up an agent may do on its own patches, how to push debugging\npatches, how to request extra CI sessions on a build, how to write\nkernel compat code, fault injection and cheap, well-sized subtests,\nwhich ZFS version to build against, and to leave master-next changes\nalone.\n\nAlso address review comments on the first patch: link the ltvm repo\nunder github.com/lustre, note that auster leaves the filesystem\nmounted after a failure, restrict skip_env to required packages, add\nbuild, test and commit-msg traps found by other developers, and ask\nfor plain English.  Add Marc Vef as a reviewer.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I9bfaad9c4e0370bea7103ba2e69649fe883ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
